<ArticleLayout slug="cost-of-social-content-week" ctaLabel="Send a brief" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">A week of social content costs about $2,200 in the US if one salaried marketer at the national median makes it, employer costs included, and anywhere from under $100 to more than $5,000 if an agency does. The spread isn't noise. Each route charges for something different, and the costs nobody quotes (review hours above all) stay with you whichever route you pick.</p>

  <h2>What is the cost of social media content creation for one week?</h2>

  <p>For the week defined below, ten posts on four networks, the cost of social media content creation runs about $2,200 for one loaded US marketing specialist, $430 to $560 for each US freelance day, and $93 to $5,400 at published agency per-post prices. In an app like hubStudio you pay per run from a prepaid balance, with every price shown first.</p>

