  <p>The freelance row moves with the days you assume, the agency row with the tier. In-house, everything turns on whether the person has other work to fill the week. None of the rows includes the costs in the next section.</p>

  <h2>What are the hidden costs of social media content?</h2>

  <p>They're the costs every route carries and no quote prints. The one all five routes share is the review.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">A US marketing manager's median wage was $80.19 an hour in May 2025, which at the June 2026 load of 1.43 is about $115 an hour to the employer.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: US Bureau of Labor Statistics, Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics, May 2025, and Employer Costs for Employee Compensation, June 2026.</p>

  <p>Each hour that manager spends briefing, reviewing and sending back the defined week costs about $115, on top of whatever route made it. If one approval round becomes three, that hour gets paid three times.</p>

