  <h2>What does the same week cost in an app?</h2>

  <p>An app has no weekly price to quote, only rules for what gets charged. hubStudio has no subscription and no seat fees, and creating an account costs nothing. You top up a prepaid balance in real currency, and each run is charged against it at the price shown before it runs.</p>

  <p>For the defined week, that means you pay for:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>The images:</strong> each run of the image studio, at the price shown first.</li>
    <li><strong>The two videos:</strong> each render of the video studio, same rule.</li>
    <li><strong>AI writing, if you use it:</strong> drafting posts with AI or improving a prompt is a paid run.</li>
    <li><strong>Posts sent to X</strong>, if X is one of your networks: each one is charged, with the price shown before you send.</li>
    <li><strong>Storage and downloads:</strong> a small charge against the balance.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>A failed run is never charged. The Image editor is free. So is Validation, where a manager or client approves work or sends it back with a comment, and so are Campaigns, which keep one launch's files under one name. Publishing to LinkedIn, Instagram, Facebook and TikTok (TikTok is in Beta) costs nothing, which covers all four networks in the defined week.</p>

  <p>What it doesn't remove is your team's time to brief and review, and the manager hour from the section above. The <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> on this site sets out the same structure, with no amounts: the price of a run appears in the app before you start it.</p>

  <h2>When does a studio make more sense than any of the four?</h2>

  <p>When the week stops being routine. A launch, a new campaign look, a product that has to be shot, or a market whose platforms you don't know: those weeks need a senior art director's judgment more than another pair of hands.</p>

  <p>hubStudio offers three ways to work, and the choice comes down to who you want making the work:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Use the app.</strong> Your team makes the week in hubStudio and pays as it goes from the prepaid balance.</li>
    <li><strong>Studio + app.</strong> Our studio makes the work inside hubStudio. Your people review, comment and approve it in Validation and their Client space, then download or publish.</li>
    <li><strong>Studio only.</strong> You send a brief and receive finished files, with no account needed.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>A producer reads every brief within one business day, and a written proposal follows within 48 hours. Studio work is quoted after the brief, as assets, a project or a retainer, and rates aren't published. The <a href="/services/design/social-media">social media design service page</a> shows the kind of work involved, the <a href="/solutions/platforms/linkedin">LinkedIn platform page</a> shows it for one network, and <a href="/resources/insights/subscription-or-managed-production">subscription or managed production</a> compares two ways of buying a steady flow of it.</p>

